00:10:53.310 --> 00:11:13.436
Now, so we have the following: all of his correspondence in Spanish. Only one single letter written addressed to a bank in Italian, which is obviously is like you know by somebody who does not control the language. But he was born in Italy. How do you explain this?

00:11:13.436 --> 00:11:42.037
Of course, if you know Jewish people, you know, must have come from those families, who were conversos, who left Spain because of the pureza de sangre. There was all laws about purity of blood. I I discuss this in my book, in my my new book. And people with who Christians that did not have pure Christian blood, were hunted and persecuted. It must have gone to Italy, and like all Jews, still kept the language of the of the whole.

00:11:42.036 --> 00:12:02.689
There is a very important point that I made several years ago at a university. He has also he writes in Latin. He has a few letters and few notes in Latin. Now, when you write a language, not only one language you write, you always make mistakes.

00:12:02.689 --> 00:12:18.869
When I write Spanish, sometimes I do make mistakes. In Hebrew, it's almost impossible for me to make mistakes because I know I cannot make mistakes in Hebrew. But when I write Spanish or English or French, I make mistakes, mispellings. Now, here's the point that I caught.

00:12:18.869 --> 00:12:33.587
And I said it. I gave it. This was at the University of Chicago, and it was very well received because it was a very meticulous analysis. The mistakes that he makes when he writes in Latin—we all make mistakes.

00:12:33.587 --> 00:12:53.427
The misspellings are misspellings which only a Spanish-speaking individual will make, not of an Italian. When you write English, if you're French, you're going to make the same mistakes that if you are German or Spanish. The mistakes that he makes, Columbus makes.

00:12:53.427 --> 00:13:18.768
When he writes in Latin, are mistakes of Spanish speaking. So here you have, I think it's almost clear, the fact that in Italian, his first language is Spanish. All right. Now, a last point. You know that eventually he was.

