01:18:46.149 --> 01:19:04.484
This lecture it touches upon the life of one of the individuals who changed literally the map of the world. Whatever is going on today.

01:19:04.484 --> 01:19:21.574
Whereas in Africa, Asia, Europe, the Moon, it is an effect of what this individual did. Why did he do it?

01:19:21.574 --> 01:19:39.523
How did it do it? What I try to show is that it was done through a group of individuals who had a vision. They believe somehow that the Book of Ezra cannot be wrong.

01:19:39.523 --> 01:20:02.197
They believe that somehow the Book of Yeshayahu cannot be wrong. There is a land to discover. That is the size of the land. They believe in the tradition of Rabbi Abraham Zacuto, Rabbi Abraham Crescas about how to navigate. They use the instrument of the Albag, Rabbi Ben Gershon.

01:20:02.197 --> 01:20:18.085
The maps of Rabbi Abraham Crescas, the almanac of Rabbi Abraham Zacuto, the money of Luis de Santangel, the influence of Gabriel Sanchez and others.

01:20:18.085 --> 01:20:37.889
To carry on a dream, the dream was: we're going to discover a new world. We're going to it's an extraordinary investment. We're going to be able to take some money, and with this money, we're going to be able to finance an army.

01:20:37.889 --> 01:21:07.832
That eventually is going to conquer us, and eventually this is going to serve as the land for all these people. That's the truth. That's the truth. It's going to die. It failed. It failed because we were living in a Christian society in which it abused, it used the Jew.

01:21:07.832 --> 01:21:35.103
But never, never kept its promises. Eventually, Columbus got zero, nothing. That's right. His children afterwards, they gave him some sort of nobility title. But I knew one of his descendants because now they belong to the nobility of the Columbus Colonies in Spain. And one of them told me.

01:21:35.103 --> 01:21:57.906
My face. We are of Jewish background. They know this. This will show how much we have done for for humanity. And in spite of everything we have done for humanity, we are not recognized. Our contribution. I need to be recognized.

01:21:57.906 --> 01:22:20.367
And I personally feel that part of the fault is ours. We are not vocal enough. We are not proud enough. We are not energized enough. And I'm sorry, we're sometimes gullible to believe all the nonsense.

01:22:20.367 --> 01:22:40.509
That historians say about Judaism. I believe very, very strongly what one of the hakamim that I mentioned in my book, Horacio de Castro says. Horacio de Castro has a fantastic idea. National histories.

01:22:40.509 --> 01:22:55.782
It's a political dimension. To deny a people the right to tell you what the national history is is to deny the people the right to live as a nation.

01:22:55.782 --> 01:23:14.373
And therefore, Raul de Castro, one of the great hakamim from Amsterdam, he believed that only the Jew could write Jewish history. No American would tolerate that somebody say the story about.

01:23:14.373 --> 01:23:38.578
Washington, cutting the will of territory is false. They will not tolerate that. Why? It's a matter of national pride. Well, those Jews from Sephard, and now it is the 500th anniversary for the expulsion of Spain. They believe that we have to have this Jewish pride.

01:23:38.578 --> 01:24:08.542
One of the things we're missing is the Jewish pride. A last point. Last point. Hopefully next year we will be inaugurating our classes, our lectures in our new building. Yes, we're building a building. The four walls already are finished. Soon they're going to start working in the interior. We're going to have services for the high holidays.

01:24:08.542 --> 01:24:22.147
But more important, the services. I want to start teaching Torah and Jewish tradition with one objective.

01:24:22.147 --> 01:24:46.423
To rekindle, to revive, we have to know our roots. We have to know our past. We have to reacquaint ourselves with ourselves. We believe in America, but we do not take advantage of it. America is a democracy.

